{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-knot-operator-basis-table-table4-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:knot-operator-basis-table-table4-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 4 from rem:knot-operator-basis-table","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-operator-basis-table"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"knot-operator-basis-table-table4-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:knot-operator-basis-table-table4-data\"></a><p>This table records, for each basis operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code>, whether it creates an electron <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code> and whether the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma</code>-conjugate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma \\cdot T \\cdot \\gamma</code> retains that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code>. The braid words are written in the generators <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code> the coefficient and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma</code> the identity operator of the Hecke relation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0^2 = h\\sigma_0 + \\gamma</code>; the \"Pairs with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^- \\neq 0</code>\" column counts, out of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">36</code>, the pairings for which <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code> is non-zero, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">36/36</code> marks an operator that always produces an electron.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Operator</th>\n<th align=\"center\">Braid word</th>\n<th align=\"center\">Pairs with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^- \\neq 0</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma \\cdot T \\cdot \\gamma</code> has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code>?</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{1,0}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{1}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">19/36</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>No</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,1}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">24/36</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>No</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,2}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0^2 = h\\sigma_0 + \\gamma</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">24/36</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>No</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,3}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0\\sigma_1\\sigma_0 = e^-</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>36/36</strong></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>Yes</strong> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">= 1</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,5}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_0\\sigma_1)^2\\sigma_0</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>36/36</strong></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>Yes</strong> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">= h^2</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-operations/knot-operator-basis-table-table4-data.md","heading":"Table"}
